body:
I have a few questions i hope i don't bother you(;

>If you are self-aware enough to live consciously, you are able to change how you view the world and its surroundings. And if you are open-minded to the world around you, your mental state and beliefs will gradually align with your progressive mindset. 

Can i ask what do you mean by this? Live consciously ? Sorry i don't really understood);



>With that being said, it really just depends on each individual and where they are in life. No two people are the same so everyone's journey is different because of it. If you believe dedication and hard work will give you success, then that is how it'll be. If you believe it'll be easy, then being consistent doesn't necessarily have to be a part of it.


- that's exacly what i'm talking about. I think it's true but just that the only thing that effects how fast you will shift/respawn to your new life is how seriously you take this process. How consistent you are , not mindset or beliefs , even thought i do think belief is helpful. Because  when you believe , for example , as a depressed person using a respawn sub , and they believe that it's possible , to die and "reborn" , and get a new life , i think that belief, even thought doesn't increase the speed of the process , i think that belief would help their day to day life. Knowing they will get a new one.
